PARITY NOTES (web components/layout/Breadcrumbs.tsx -> native)
================================================================================
- Props: items[BreadcrumbItem{label,href?}], homeHref('/'), homeAriaLabel -> faithfully ported.
- items.length <= 1 => render nothing (self-suppress)                 -> resolved.isSuppressed => EmptyView()
- nav aria-label t('a11y.breadcrumb','Breadcrumb')                    -> breadcrumbs.a11y.nav
- Home link homeAriaLabel ?? t('a11y.breadcrumbHome','Dashboard')     -> breadcrumbs.a11y.home, SF Symbol "house"
- chevron separator (aria-hidden)                                     -> SF Symbol "chevron.right", accessibilityHidden
- isLast || !href => plain text (last = secondary+medium, else muted) -> role currentLeaf / plainText
- !isLast && href => link (PrefetchLink)                              -> role link, Button + .isLink trait
- truncate max-w-[200px]                                              -> lineLimit(1)+truncationMode(.tail)+frame(maxW:200)
- middle items "hidden sm:inline" + mobile "..." (responsive collapse)-> idiomatic horizontal ScrollView
  (every crumb reachable; data/order/links/truncation/suppression preserved; documented adaptation,
  matching accepted predecessor 0166). The web source does NO fetch -> no loading/error/stale/offline
  states exist to reproduce; inventing them would contradict the source (documented in Adapter header).
- Tokens P1/S9 only (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing); no Tailwind ports, no raw hex.
